# Rendered by the Maran agent. Hand edits are overwritten on the next apply.
#
# The `header_checks` table of the `cleanup_local` service, the one only `pickup`
# feeds (master.cf). Postfix never shows a milter the Received line pickup writes
# ("Received: by <host> (Postfix, from userid <uid>)", first in the message), and
# that line is the only place the real uid of the submitting user is recorded. The
# table copies the uid and the maildrop id out of it into a header the milter does
# see, which the Rspamd local-submission rule reads (issue #518,
# docs/mail/local-submission.md).
#
# PREPEND puts the new header before the line that matched, and pickup's line is the
# first one, so the header made here is the topmost of its name. A line of the same
# shape written by the sender comes later and makes a header below it; the rule
# trusts only the topmost. `mail_name` is pinned to Postfix in main.cf because it is
# the text matched here.
/^Received: by [^ ]+ \(Postfix, from userid ([0-9]+)\)[[:space:]]+id ([0-9A-Za-z]+);/ PREPEND X-Maran-Local-Submitter: $1 $2
